\u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Infrastructure schemes delayed by procurement and contract specification issues totalling over \u00a31.5m","lead":"Multiple infrastructure schemes held back by procurement and tendering delays indicate systematic project delivery challenges and suggest the council may face cost inflation if these schemes extend further into higher cost periods.","iso":"2026-09-02","paper_title":"Appendix F6 - Details of capital slippage","paper_url":"https://moderngov.middlesbrough.gov.uk/documents/s44747/44747.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Broadcasting House repairs delayed by technical challenges with rooftop aerials, pushing \u00a31.497m into 2027/28","lead":"Technical delays on capital projects indicate delivery challenges and are a visible signal of project governance capability, which lenders assess when evaluating the council's ability to manage large capital schemes and borrowing.","iso":"2026-09-02","paper_title":"Appendix F6 - Details of capital slippage","paper_url":"https://moderngov.middlesbrough.gov.uk/documents/s44747/44747.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-02","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Appendix F6 - Details of capital slippage","paper_url":"https://moderngov.middlesbrough.gov.uk/documents/s44747/44747.pdf","headline":"\u00a31.5m ICT Transformational programme deferred with no clear explanation of revised timescale","detail":"The council's ICT Transformational Capital Expenditure programme (funded from capital receipts) is slipping from 2026/27 into 2027/28 because transformational activities are not expected to proceed on the original schedule. No explanation is provided for the change in timescale or when the work is now expected.","category":"capital","matters":"A major strategic capital programme being reprofiled without clear justification raises questions about strategic planning certainty and the council's ability to execute digital transformation, which affects longer-term operational efficiency.","figures":"\u00a31.5m originally planned for 2026/27","quote":"Transformational activities are not expected to take place in accordance with the original timescales","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-02","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Appendix F6 - Details of capital slippage","paper_url":"https://moderngov.middlesbrough.gov.uk/documents/s44747/44747.pdf","headline":"Infrastructure schemes delayed by procurement and contract specification issues totalling over \u00a31.5m","detail":"Highways maintenance (\u00a30.5m), Bridges & Structures (\u00a31.0m), and Investment/Commercial Properties improvements (\u00a30.3m) are all reprofiled due to procurement delays or contract specification issues. The Highways and Bridges delays cite the same cause: procurement-related difficulties.","category":"capital","matters":"Multiple infrastructure schemes held back by procurement and tendering delays indicate systematic project delivery challenges and suggest the council may face cost inflation if these schemes extend further into higher cost periods.","figures":"Highways \u00a30.5m, Bridges & Structures \u00a31.0m, Investment/Commercial Properties \u00a30.3m","quote":"Larger carriageway repair schemes are likely to be delayed due to procurement-related issues, resulting in the rephasing of associated expenditure within the capital programme","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-02","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Appendix F6 - Details of capital slippage","paper_url":"https://moderngov.middlesbrough.gov.uk/documents/s44747/44747.pdf","headline":"Broadcasting House repairs delayed by technical challenges with rooftop aerials, pushing \u00a31.497m into 2027/28","detail":"The Broadcasting House capital project has encountered technical challenges in relocating rooftop aerials, delaying the scheme and reprofiling \u00a31.497m of borrowing-funded expenditure from 2026/27 into 2027/28. This represents a material delay on a major capital investment.","category":"capital","matters":"Technical delays on capital projects indicate delivery challenges and are a visible signal of project governance capability, which lenders assess when evaluating the council's ability to manage large capital schemes and borrowing.","figures":"\u00a31.497m, deferred from 2026/27 to 2027/28","quote":"Progress on the project has been delayed as a result of technical challenges related to the relocation of the rooftop aerials.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-02","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Appendix F5 - New, Additions and Virements to Capital","paper_url":"https://moderngov.middlesbrough.gov.uk/documents/s44746/44746.pdf","headline":"Depot refurbishment scheme has identified additional costs mid-delivery","detail":"The council is reallocating unspent funding from the Resolution House project to cover 'additional costs identified during the delivery of the programme' for the depot refurbishment. This indicates the original budget for the scheme was insufficient and required mid-project reforecasting.","category":"overspend","matters":"Capital project cost overruns mid-delivery suggest budget control weaknesses and pressure on the capital programme to absorb unexpected costs.","figures":"\u00a30.276 million reallocated to cover additional costs","quote":"Unspent capital funding from the Resolution House project will be reallocated to the depot refurbishment scheme, where additional costs have been identified during the delivery of the programme.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-02","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Appendix F5 - New, Additions and Virements to Capital","paper_url":"https://moderngov.middlesbrough.gov.uk/documents/s44746/44746.pdf","headline":"Middlesbrough College investment will generate no rental income, contrary to prior expectations","detail":"The council had allocated \u00a31.6m for a college extension with expectations of generating additional rental income. The college has now secured alternative funding and the council funding is not needed. As a result, 'the Council will no longer be able to generate the additional rental income previously anticipated.' The funding is being reallocated to other purposes.","category":"income","matters":"Anticipated rental income that does not materialise affects the council's revenue position and its capacity to self-fund capital investment.","figures":"\u00a31.600 million","quote":"Middlesbrough College has advised that Council funding is no longer required for the proposed extension, as alternative funding sources have been secured and as a result, the Council will no longer be able to generate the additional rental income previously anticipated.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-02"},"name":"Middlesbrough UA","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-26","since_iso":"2026-08-27","distress":false,"headline":"\u00a31.5m ICT Transformational programme deferred with no clear explanation of revised timescale","lead":"A major strategic capital programme being reprofiled without clear justification raises questions about strategic planning certainty and the council's ability to execute digital transformation, which affects longer-term operational efficiency.","also":["41 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Adult Social Care and Health Scrutiny Panel on 2026-09-29","n_findings":42,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Appendix F6 - Details of capital slippage","top_paper_url":"https://moderngov.middlesbrough.gov.uk/documents/s44747/44747.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":99,"news_drafts_total":3}}